# Docker's ignore patterns use Go filepath.Match: a leading `*` matches only at
# the root, so `*.tsbuildinfo` does NOT match `apps/api/tsbuildinfo`. Every
# pattern below is therefore `**`-prefixed.
#
# This is not a tidiness rule. A local `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` copied into the
# image tells `tsc -b` the project is already built, so it emits nothing and
# exits 0 — a green build that produces no dist. It cost a red container build
# to find; the failure at least surfaced as a missing COPY rather than a stale
# image shipping old code.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.env
.env.local
**/.DS_Store
infra/.terraform
# Model transcripts from the environments' runs. Never in an image: the Gym the
# API serves carries no recorded attempts (docs/decisions.md, "The Gym is in
# the ops console, without its recorded attempts"). `**/` so a checkout's
# worktrees, each with a runs/ of its own, are kept out too.
**/packages/environments/runs
# Claude Code's local state, worktrees among it: whole checkouts, nothing an
# image reads.
.claude
